  "body": "In https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/595#issuecomment-178357291 the suggestion came up to use a unified dictionary for all rendering contexts rather than have each rendering context define their own. Chrome already does this. This is observably different from what we do today as the IDL layer consults each object member which triggers getters. So we either all accept this or Chrome will have to change to the existing pattern.\r\n\r\n(If we expose `getContextAttributes()` on more rendering contexts as tracked by #3182 we'd still create specific dictionaries for each rendering context there, returning only the members that make sense.)\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/canvas ",
